When generating a Git commit message for this repository (including the Source Control sparkle button), use EXACTLY this conventional format. One short subject line. No quotes around the message.

```text
fix(core): keep decorations when showing hidden main window
feat(cli): add --no-tui flag for CI logs
docs: clarify app.start setup for contributors
```

Rules:
- Format: `type(scope): subject` or `type: subject` when no package fits
- Types: feat, fix, docs, chore, refactor, test, ci, style
- Scopes: core, cli, native, registry, client, react, vite, or omit
- Subject: lowercase, imperative, no trailing period, one line
- Never write a sentence like "Enhance X and add Y for improved Z"

Examples for this repo:
- docs: add Biome lint rules to the contributing guide
- ci: run Biome on changed files in pull requests
- chore: add pnpm validate for local PR checks
